// Hostomel, sub-chapter I, The landing (Десант): 24 February 2022, late morning. About 34 helicopters bring 200-300
// VDV of the 31st Air Assault and 45th Spetsnaz Brigades onto the field; fewer than 200 National Guard conscripts
// of the 4th Rapid Reaction Brigade's rear echelon hold them for more than an hour, then pull out, out of ammunition
// (c01 §2 the timeline, §4, §6 set piece 2). The schema is bav_core::data and bav_sim::data; the map is map.ron.
//
// Phase 1 of design/hostomel.md: the field and the clock. The helicopters, the infantry fight and the Igla come in
// phases 2 to 4; until then the attack's lines below are set so nothing in the column game fires.
(
    // 10:20 to about 13:05 in the day's 1500 s: the stream crosses the Kyiv dam about 10:30 and is over the field
    // about 11:00; the defenders are out by 13:00.
    day_start_min: 620.0,
    compression: 0.11,
    attacker: Ru,
    // Fictional, the National Guard's: the player (viburnum), the D-30s at Horenka (mace), the observers on the
    // tower (tower), the battalion's command post (oak).
    callsigns: (player: ("Kalyna", "Калина"), guns: ("Bulava", "Булава"), op: ("Vezha", "Вежа"), command: ("Dub", "Дуб")),
    words: (
        briefing: r#"HOSTOMEL (ГОСТОМЕЛЬ), ANTONOV AIRPORT
24 FEBRUARY 2022, LATE MORNING

At four this morning Russia invaded. At dawn Kalibr missiles hit this airfield and the National Guard's base
beside it. The airport has a 3.5 km runway, 25 km from Kyiv: whoever holds it can fly an army in.

The 4th Rapid Reaction Brigade (4-та бригада оперативного призначення НГУ) has gone east. Its rear echelon is
left: fewer than two hundred conscripts, with rifles, a few BTRs, Igla missiles and one ZU-23-2.
Two D-30 howitzers stand at Horenka (Горенка).

Helicopters are coming down the Dnipro. Dozens of them.

The day will run whether or not you do anything. What you do decides how long the field holds.

Mouse: right-drag to look, wheel to zoom.  WASD: fly the drone.  Q/E: turn.  R/F: climb/descend.
Left click: the D-30s at Horenka.  1/2 or Tab: drone / the tower.  P: pause.  [ ]: time.

Press Enter."#,
        op_label: "OBSERVERS, THE CONTROL TOWER (СПОСТЕРІГАЧІ, ДИСПЕТЧЕРСЬКА ВЕЖА)",
        op_lost: "The tower is hit. No eyes over the apron.",
        forward_belt: "the apron",
        plow_mine: "",
        mine_lines: [""],
        registered: ("", "Bulava firing on the runway."),
        closing: [
            "The airlift that was to follow, eighteen Il-76s with the 76th Air Assault Division, turned back in the air.",
            "At dusk the army came back for the field (the counterattack, the next part).",
        ],
        keys: "R: the same morning again.     Esc: quit.",
        sources: [
            (publisher: "The Washington Post", date: "24 Aug 2022", title: "Battle for Kyiv: Ukrainian valor, Russian blunders combined to save the capital", url: "https://www.washingtonpost.com/national-security/interactive/2022/kyiv-battle-ukraine-survival/"),
            (publisher: "RUSI", date: "7 Nov 2022", title: "The Russian air war and Ukrainian requirements for air defence", url: "https://www.rusi.org/explore-our-research/publications/special-resources/russian-air-war-and-ukrainian-requirements-air-defence"),
            (publisher: "RUSI", date: "30 Nov 2022", title: "Preliminary lessons in conventional warfighting from Russia's invasion of Ukraine: February–July 2022", url: "https://www.rusi.org/explore-our-research/publications/special-resources/preliminary-lessons-conventional-warfighting-russias-invasion-ukraine-february-july-2022"),
            (publisher: "War on the Rocks", date: "10 Aug 2023", title: "The battle of Hostomel airport: a key moment in Russia's defeat in Kyiv", url: "https://warontherocks.com/the-battle-of-hostomel-airport-a-key-moment-in-russias-defeat-in-kyiv/"),
            (publisher: "The British Army Review", date: "Mar 2024", title: "The battle of Irpin River, February/March 2022", url: "https://chacr.org.uk/wp-content/uploads/2024/03/BAR-187-compressed.pdf"),
            (publisher: "Modern War Institute", date: "21 Feb 2025", title: "Urban Warfare Project case study #12: battle of Kyiv", url: "https://mwi.westpoint.edu/urban-warfare-project-case-study-12-battle-of-kyiv/"),
        ],
    ),
    // Over the apron, looking west at the runway.
    camera: (900.0, 450.0),
    observed_from: Home,

    // The National Guard's posts (c01 §3): the hangar, the apron's north end, the stands, the tower and offices,
    // and the base's gate by the railway crossing. Where the radar stood the sources do not place; here it is at the
    // runway's south end (an assumption, flagged in design/hostomel.md).
    ua_positions: [(990.0, 610.0), (700.0, 330.0), (800.0, 700.0), (1000.0, 1100.0), (1250.0, 560.0), (520.0, 1000.0)],
    ru_positions: [],
    routes: [
        (line: "e373", deploy: (1030.0, -713.0), objective: (1600.0, 450.0)),
    ],
    // The column game's lines, out of the way until the areas replace them (phase 3).
    grey_zone: (4000.0, 4500.0),
    advance: 1.0,
    foothold_z: 9000.0,
    defence_z: 9000.0,
    home: (1450.0, 760.0),
    jam_z: 9000.0,
    mortar_band: (0.0, 0.0),

    // ---- The battle's part (bav_sim::data) ----
    catalog: [],
    support: [],
    allotment: (points: 0, record: []),
    old_wreck_kinds: [],
    space_key: Atgm,
    shift_fire: Raam,
    registered_fire: (600.0, 0),
    operator: (pos: (1450.0, 760.0), found_per_hour: 0.0),
    script: [
        (2.0, Say("Bird up. Low cloud, drizzle. The hangars are still smoking from this morning's missiles.")),
        (12.0, Say("All, this is {command}. Helicopters over the Kyiv dam, coming up the river. Many of them. To your posts.")),
    ],
)
